## It was the tool's — and I fixed the tool

R10 got to "KLayout deep mode splits an 18-vertex polygon and measures to the cut". I reproduced that independently, then got the engine to hand me the offending edge pair — `(1065,1310;1215,1310)/(1065,1235;1215,1235)`, subject edge sitting exactly on the split line — and instrumented a build to find why:

```
[KLDBG] subjects=1 primary_intruders=0 ... BRANCH=2_merge_subjects
```

`check_local_operation::override_distance()` sets the foreign pseudo-intruder search enlargement to `0` with a comment saying "only touching". KLayout's own header: **`1` is touching; `0` is overlap**. Split fragments share exactly an edge — boxes touch, never overlap — so the sibling never arrives, the subject-merging compensation does nothing, and the cut becomes a polygon boundary. One character.

**[vibeic/klayout#2](https://github.com/vibeic/klayout/pull/2)** — with a unit test that fails on the parent commit and passes on the branch, plus a three-binary deck table: distribution 8 violations, my unpatched build 8 (same report size to the byte), patched build 0. The 7 `li.5` inside foundry std cells were the same defect — shown with the **distribution binary**, no build of mine involved.

